From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v8: Add Chromium compiler-rt headers for Clang builds

The Yocto toolchain uses a system Clang, while V8 enables its sanitizer
interfaces when sanitizer hardening flags are present. Unlike Chromium's
bundled Clang, the system compiler does not implicitly expose Chromium's
compiler-rt headers, which makes sanitizer/common_interface_defs.h
unavailable when compiling V8.

Expose the in-tree compiler-rt include directory through V8's internal
configuration for Clang builds.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 v8/BUILD.gn | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/BUILD.gn b/v8/BUILD.gn
--- a/v8/BUILD.gn
+++ b/v8/BUILD.gn
@@ -901,2 +901,6 @@
   ]
+  if (is_clang) {
+    include_dirs += [ "//third_party/compiler-rt/src/include" ]
+  }
+
 }
